aad18b9b517684c5e529d8076d2e67219b66e2429494bcf585d4cb","file":"preprints/A-counterexample-to-Hadwigers-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":48,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"a57113eb99239bff4468d2064c28bd99e2c99e0100f1c84d51c54e54a09f1e9c","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-counterexample-to-Hadwigers-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:848d5b4f06aad18b9b517684c5e529d8076d2e67219b66e2429494bcf585d4cb","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-counterexample-to-Hadwigers-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L48"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:hadwiger}\\label{cor:fractional-hadwiger}\nThere are finite nonempty simple graphs \\(G\\) of arbitrarily large\norder \\(m\\) for which\n\\[\n h(G)<\\frac{26m}{75}+\\frac23\n <\\frac m2\\le\\chi_f(G)\\le\\chi(G).\n\\]\nThus Hadwiger's conjecture and its fractional-coloring weakening\n\\(\\chi_f(G)\\le h(G)\\) are false."}
